      "text": "Ukraine's State Online Monitoring System has moved from concept to live operation, with the first 11 licensed operators connected and transmitting transaction data to the state in close to real time - recording bets, returns, winnings and other operations rather than relying on periodic reporting packs. PlayCity, the state agency for gambling and lottery oversight headed by Hennadii Novikov since April 2025, has issued 11 operator licences, three lottery licences and 213 gaming-equipment supplier licences, roughly 250 in its first year, alongside aggressive enforcement against unlicensed supply. Phase 2 of SOMS is being implemented now, with December 2026 targeted for full integration of land-based and online monitoring. The engineering demand here is different in kind from a regulatory reporting module. Continuous transaction streaming means the platform needs an event bus that can emit at wager granularity without degrading in-play latency, schema versioning that survives a regulator changing its field definitions mid-year, replay and reconciliation for gaps, and a clear answer to what happens to the customer journey when the state endpoint is unavailable. Ukraine joins a lengthening list - Romania, Greece, Colombia, Peru and the Philippines all now expect some flavour of near-live data - which argues for treating regulator streaming as a first-class, configurable platform capability rather than a per-market integration project delivered by a market-entry squad.",
